    "title": "Novak Djokovic Defeats Francesco Maestrelli in Australian Open Second Round",
    "text": "• Novak Djokovic defeated Francesco Maestrelli in the second round of the Australian Open.\n• Djokovic won with a score of 6-3, 6-2, 6-2.\n• Maestrelli is a qualifier and this was only his second main draw match at a Grand Slam.\n• Djokovic acknowledged Maestrelli's serve and commended the young Italian.\n• Djokovic's next opponent is likely Botic van de Zandschulp in the third round.\n• The match was played on Rod Laver Arena.\n• Djokovic has won the Australian Open a record 10 times.\n• The article mentions other matches, including Karolina Pliskova, Taylah Preston, Maddison Inglis, Rinky Hijikata, Dane Sweeny, Lorenzo Musetti, Luciano Darderi, Amanda Anisimova, Jessica Pegula, and Madison Keys.\n• The weather in Melbourne was cool with a stiff breeze.\n• Djokovic is aiming for his 25th Grand Slam title.",
